DATA

This library reads, and may redistribute samples of, data published by
SlaveVoyages (https://www.slavevoyages.org), a collaborative project
hosted by Rice University with Emory University, the Hutchins Center at
Harvard University, the National Museum of African American History and
Culture, the Omohundro Institute, and others.

Data transcribed from historical documents is in the public domain.
Imputed data (marked * on slavevoyages.org) and all data in the
Estimates database are licensed by SlaveVoyages under a Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/). Any redistribution
of those fields, including the fixture samples in this repository,
must retain this notice and credit SlaveVoyages as the original source.

Place coordinates in src/voyages/schema/reference/curated/place_coordinates.csv
come from two sources, recorded per row in coord_source / coord_ref:
- the SlaveVoyages legacy site (github.com/IQSS/voyages), and
- GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org), licensed under Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Recommended citation:

  SlaveVoyages, Trans-Atlantic Slave Trade Database,
  https://www.slavevoyages.org (accessed <date>).

See `voyages.citation()` for the per-dataset citation string.
